              <!-- Accordion Boxes -->
              <div class="faq-container">
                <div class="faq-box open">
                  <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-0">
                    <h3>When should I take my child to the dentist for the first time?</h3>
                  </button>
                  <div class="answer" id="answer-0">
                    <p>We recommend the first check-up when the first tooth breaks through, typically between the 6th and 8th month of life. Afterward, we recommend visits every 3 to 6 months. While this sounds very early to some, it ensures children grow up routine-oriented and completely free from fear. Parents receive guidance on nutrition, brushing, fluoride use, pacifiers, bottles, or thumb-sucking habits.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="faq-box">
                  <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-1">
                    <h3>Why should I choose a specialized pediatric dental practice?</h3>
                  </button>
                  <div class="answer" id="answer-1">
                    <p>Children differ substantially from adults both anatomically and psychologically. A pediatric dental visit should be as natural as visiting a pediatrician. Treatment concepts must be tailored to their developmental stages so children experience gentle, uplifting visits and mature into fear-free adults who feel comfortable at the dentist.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="faq-box">
                  <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-2">
                    <h3>May I book an appointment without a doctor's referral?</h3>
                  </button>
                  <div class="answer" id="answer-2">
                    <p>Of course! We assess our young patients during the initial consultation and discuss all options openly and transparently with parents. A sympathetic, respectful dialogue on equal footing is our guiding principle.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="faq-box">
                  <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-3">
                    <h3>Can I book an appointment online for my child?</h3>
                  </button>
                  <div class="answer" id="answer-3">
                    <p>For first appointments, we recommend giving our practice a call so our reception team can clarify initial questions with you directly. If your child is already a patient with us and you simply need the next check-up or prophylaxis appointment, you are very welcome to use our online booking system!</p>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="faq-box">
                  <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-4">
                    <h3>Do decayed baby teeth really need to be treated?</h3>
                  </button>
                  <div class="answer" id="answer-4">
                    <p>Yes. Healthy milk teeth are essential for speech development, smiling, and relaxed chewing. Furthermore, baby teeth act as vital placeholders for the adult teeth following behind. Early loss can cause misalignment, crowding, or orthodontic complications, and untreated decay can infect developing adult teeth.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="faq-box">
                  <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-5">
                    <h3>How can we best reach the clinic?</h3>
                  </button>
                  <div class="answer" id="answer-5">
                    <p>Our Practice &amp; Clinic for Jaw &amp; Facial Medicine is conveniently located in the "CityCenter" Böblingen, Wolfgang-Brumme-Allee 25, right beside the "Mercaden" shopping center. 27 free underground parking spaces are reserved for dental clinic patients, with direct barrier-free elevator access. Böblingen train station (S-Bahn S1 &amp; S60 lines) and the central bus station are just 200 meters away.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Final Overview & CTA Section -->
        <section class="end">
          <div class="wrapper">
            <div class="contact-container fade-in">
              <h2><strong>For small, medium, and big teeth:&nbsp;Your practice &amp; clinic for children and families.</strong></h2>
              <p>In our specialized pediatric clinic, our dedicated team works with passion to make dental visits an easy, reassuring experience. In cheerfully colored rooms, friendly smiles welcome every child. We partner with parents to ensure ideal oral wellness through gentle preventive treatments, child-friendly therapies, and holistic consultations for both public and private insurance patients alike.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Check-up Examinations:</strong> Regular screenings to detect cavities early and guide oral development gently.</li>
                <li><strong>Prophylaxis &amp; Cleanings:</strong> Professional dental polishing, fluoride treatments, and fissure sealants.</li>
                <li><strong>Gentle Tooth Restorations:</strong> Child-adapted fillings, aesthetic milk tooth crowns, and pain-free treatments.</li>
                <li><strong>Orthodontic Diagnostics:</strong> Early detection of malocclusions in close collaboration with orthodontists.</li>
                <li><strong>Fear-Free Treatments:</strong> Calming behavioral guidance and optional procedures under pediatric anesthesia.</li>
              </ul>
              <p>Appointments can be booked conveniently by phone or online. Feel free to contact us – we look forward to accompanying you and your child on the journey to healthy teeth and bright, confident smiles!</p>
              <a href="#contact" class="button">
                <span>Book Appointment Now</span>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
